IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-cgt`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997, ss 102-5, 104-10, 104-215, 110-36(1A), 114-10, 115-10 to 115-102, 118-60, 118-110, 118-150, 128-10, 152-10, 152-15 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_income-tax-assessment-act-1997_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`Byford (c080)` MEANS DwellingSale WITH
    `main residence from acquisition` IS FALSE
    `months from acquisition before it became the main residence` IS 17
    `main residence from then until the sale` IS TRUE
    `built on the land and moved in as soon as practicable` IS TRUE
    `lived in for at least 3 months` IS TRUE
    `chooses section 118-150` IS TRUE
    `inherited or held as trustee of an estate` IS FALSE
    `excluded foreign resident or failing the life events test` IS FALSE

`Byford without the choice` MEANS DwellingSale WITH
    `main residence from acquisition` IS FALSE
    `months from acquisition before it became the main residence` IS 17
    `main residence from then until the sale` IS TRUE
    `built on the land and moved in as soon as practicable` IS TRUE
    `lived in for at least 3 months` IS TRUE
    `chooses section 118-150` IS FALSE
    `inherited or held as trustee of an estate` IS FALSE
    `excluded foreign resident or failing the life events test` IS FALSE

`the East Perth apartment (d055)` MEANS DwellingSale WITH
    `main residence from acquisition` IS TRUE
    `months from acquisition before it became the main residence` IS 0
    `main residence from then until the sale` IS FALSE
    `built on the land and moved in as soon as practicable` IS FALSE
    `lived in for at least 3 months` IS FALSE
    `chooses section 118-150` IS FALSE
    `inherited or held as trustee of an estate` IS FALSE
    `excluded foreign resident or failing the life events test` IS FALSE

§ `ss 110-36(1A), 114-10`

-- d071: Daniel's Jarrah shares, held from 2031-03-15 to the sale on 2050-06-30: indexed. c085: Chloe's shares from
-- 2034-02-01: indexed. A sale on 2026-06-30 is before 1 July 2027: not under (1A).
#ASSERT `Is my cost base indexed` `an individual` FALSE 20310315 20500630
#ASSERT `Is my cost base indexed` `an individual` FALSE 20340201 20500630
#ASSERT NOT `Is my cost base indexed` `an individual` FALSE 20200101 20260630

§ `s 104-10(4) with indexation`

-- d071, on hypothetical figures: proceeds 20,000,000, cost base 1,000, indexation factor 1.5: 20,000,000 - 1,500.
#ASSERT `What is my capital gain` `an individual` FALSE 20310315 20500630 20000000 1000 1.5 EQUALS 19998500

§ `ss 115-10 to 115-25`

-- d071: once the cost base is indexed the gain is not a discount capital gain (s 115-20); without indexation it would be.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my gain a discount capital gain` `an individual` 20310315 20500630 TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my gain a discount capital gain` `an individual` 20310315 20500630 FALSE

§ `ss 115-100, 115-102`

-- d071 and c085: an individual's gain from a CGT event on 30 June 2050 gets 0%, not the 50% the scenarios expect.
-- Before 1 July 2027, 50%. A new residential dwelling keeps 50% after it.
#ASSERT `What is my discount percentage` `an individual` 20500630 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is my discount percentage` `an individual` 20260630 FALSE EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `What is my discount percentage` `an individual` 20500630 TRUE EQUALS 50

§ `s 102-5`

-- A hypothetical gain of 1,000,000: at 0% all of it; at 50%, half.
#ASSERT `What is my net capital gain` 1000000 0 0 EQUALS 1000000
#ASSERT `What is my net capital gain` 1000000 0 50 EQUALS 500000

§ `ss 118-110, 118-150`

-- c080: Byford, land bought 17 months before Chloe and Liam moved in on handover: exempt only with the s 118-150 choice.
-- d055: Daniel and Priya's East Perth apartment, lived in from purchase: exempt.
#ASSERT `Is the gain on my home disregarded` `Byford (c080)`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the gain on my home disregarded` `Byford without the choice`
#ASSERT `Is the gain on my home disregarded` `the East Perth apartment (d055)`

§ `ss 152-10(1)(c), 152-15`

-- d071: Jarrah sold for $40,000,000; net value taken as that figure (an inference): condition (c) fails. At $6,000,000 it is met.
#ASSERT NOT `Do I meet basic condition (c)` FALSE 0 40000000 FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I meet basic condition (c)` FALSE 0 6000000 FALSE

§ `ss 128-10, 104-215, 118-60`

-- d093: the residue to the testamentary trust (resident trustee) -- no gain; the gift by will to the Foundation (exempt
-- entity) -- K3 would happen, but s 118-60(1) disregards it; the same asset to an exempt entity other than as such a gift -- a gain.
#ASSERT NOT `Does my death make a capital gain` `an Australian resident individual or ordinary trust` 20380520 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my death make a capital gain` `an exempt entity` 20400101 TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my death make a capital gain` `an exempt entity` 20400101 FALSE

